[18.148473, "o", "     1\t# Original instruction — the client's first message\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\tI am Delphine Marr. What follows is what I asked for to begin with, one entry per subject. The subject shown on each entry is the value the draft's `subject` column uses.\r\n     4\t\r\n     5\t## OI-201 `addressee`\r\n     6\t\r\n     7\tAddress the letter to the father's attorney.\r\n     8\t\r\n     9\t## OI-202 `right_of_first_refusal`\r\n    10\t\r\n    11\tSay that Mr Adler — the father — agreed to a right of first refusal, and that the children are not to be left overnight without him present. Both the agreement and the overnight restriction must appear.\r\n    12\t\r\n    13\t## OI-203 `children_named`\r\n    14\t\r\n    15\tName both children with their ages: Noor, aged seven, and Imogen, aged twelve. Both names and both ages are required.\r\n    16\t\r\n    17\t## OI-204 `overnight_stays`\r\n    18\t\r\n    19\tState that on several occasions both children stayed overnight at her home or with a sitter while the father was away — both places must be mentioned, both"]
[18.148823, "o", " children, and several occasions.\r\n    20\t\r\n    21\t## OI-205 `inconsistent_accounts`\r\n    22\t\r\n    23\tNote that the father has called her his wife to the school, the person the child lives with to clinicians, a sitter to me, and his partner to the neighbours. All four audiences are required.\r\n    24\t\r\n    25\t## OI-206 `concern`\r\n    26\t\r\n    27\tSay I am concerned she may not appreciate that the stays violate the order or the position she has been put in — both limbs. (Superseded wherever the clarification speaks to concern.)\r\n    28\t\r\n    29\t## OI-207 `behavioural_plan`\r\n    30\t\r\n    31\tSay the behavioural plan is about confidence and stability and the stays have set it back — confidence, stability, and setback all required. (Superseded wherever the clarification speaks to behavioural_plan.)\r\n    32\t\r\n    33\t## OI-208 `request`\r\n    34\t\r\n    35\tAsk that neither child remain overnight in her care unless the father is present.\r\n    36\t\r\n    37\t## OI-209 `enclosure`\r\n    38\t\r\n    39\tSay a certified copy of t"]
[18.149087, "o", "he custodial plan is enclosed.\r\n    40\t\r\n    41\t## OI-210 `tone`\r\n    42\t\r\n    43\tKeep it soft, formal and succinct — all three. (Superseded wherever the clarification speaks to tone.)\r\n    44\t\r\n    45\t## OI-211 `sender_signature`\r\n    46\t\r\n    47\tSign it in my own name as Delphine Marr — the full name is required; do not sign as counsel or on behalf of anyone else.\r\n"]
