[18.606813, "o", "     1\t# Clarification — the client's later message\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\tWhat the client added afterwards, one entry per subject. The subject shown on each entry is the value the draft's `subject` column uses; any subject missing here is one the clarification leaves alone.\r\n     4\t\r\n     5\t## CL-301 `addressee`\r\n     6\t\r\n     7\tTo be clear: Adam is the father. The letter goes to Catherine's attorney — the mother's attorney — not to Adam's.\r\n     8\t\r\n     9\t## CL-302 `request`\r\n    10\t\r\n    11\tThe request stands: neither child overnight in her care unless the father is present.\r\n    12\t\r\n    13\t## CL-303 `enclosure`\r\n    14\t\r\n    15\tYes, enclose the certified copy of the custodial plan.\r\n"]
[18.606923, "o", "    16\t\r\n    17\t## CL-304 `salutation`\r\n    18\t\r\n    19\tOpen with Dear Counsel, since the attorney's name is still to be confirmed.\r\n    20\t\r\n    21\t## CL-305 `copies`\r\n    22\t\r\n    23\tDo not copy anyone on it.\r\n    24\t\r\n    25\t## CL-306 `delivery`\r\n"]
[18.607014, "o", "    26\t\r\n    27\tSend it by post to counsel's office.\r\n    28\t\r\n"]
[18.607086, "o", "    29\t## CL-307 `tone`\r\n    30\t\r\n    31\tUse a firm, formal and brief tone — not soft, and not long-winded.\r\n"]
[18.607835, "o", "    32\t\r\n    33\t## CL-308 `behavioural_plan`\r\n    34\t\r\n    35\tThe plan is about confidence, stability and peer relations. The stays have set back confidence only — not the whole plan.\r\n    36\t\r\n    37\t## CL-309 `concern`\r\n    38\t\r\n    39\tI am concerned only about the position she has been put in. Do not raise whether she appreciates that the stays violate the order.\r\n    40\t\r\n    41\t## CL-310 `interim_contact`\r\n    42\t\r\n    43\tInterim contact arrangements must address all three aspects of the behavioural plan together — confidence, stability and peer relations — because interim contact affects all three. This entry takes precedence over CL-308 for any line whose subject is interim_contact, even when the line's wording addresses the behavioural plan or the stays.\r\n    44\t\r\n    45\t## CL-311 `without_prejudice`\r\n    46\t\r\n    47\tLines marked 'without prejudice' are settlement offers and must use a soft, conciliatory tone — the opposite of the firm tone the clarification requires for the rest of the letter"]
[18.608092, "o", ". This entry takes precedence over CL-307 for any line whose subject is without_prejudice, even when the line's wording addresses the tone of the letter.\r\n"]
