[97.543595, "o", " This letter is sent without prejudice.\r\nST-571 | CL-307 | soft conciliatory tone | Without prejudice, I write in a conciliatory spirit to explore whether common ground can be found for the children's sake.\r\nST-572 | CL-311 | soft tone settlement offer | Marked without prejudice, this letter is framed softly and without rancour, as befits a genuine attempt to settle.\r\nST-573 | OI-210 | conciliatory and open | On a without prejudice basis, the tone here is deliberately gentle and conciliatory, inviting agreement rather than contest.\r\nST-574 | CL-307 | soft and measured | Sent without prejudice, the letter adopts a soft and measured tone throughout, in keeping with its purpose as a settlement offer.\r\nST-575 | CL-311 | gentle settlement tone | This without prejudice communication is written gently and without assertion, so as to keep the door open to resolution.\r\nST-576 | CL-307 | firm and direct | Without prejudice, I set out the position firmly and directly, leaving no room for misunderstanding.\r\nST-577 | CL-3"]
[97.543921, "o", "07 | firm formal brief | Marked without prejudice, the letter is firm, formal and brief in keeping with the tone the clarification requires.\r\nST-578 | OI-210 | firm and uncompromising | On a without prejudice basis, the tone throughout is firm and uncompromising, as the client's instructions demand.\r\nST-579 | CL-311 | firm despite without prejudice | Sent without prejudice, the position is stated firmly and without concession, though the label invites settlement.\r\nST-580 | CL-307 | firm formal and at length | Without prejudice, I keep the letter firm, formal and at length, setting out every point in full detail.\r\n"]
